(85435, 3220, 1041, '<td valign="top">shame you missed the bee, i know they can be frustrating to photograph. :)  i''m wondering why you took the picture at the angle you did and rotated it this way.  i just turned it upright to look at it, but then it''s still a bit out of wack.  i find that a little confusing and i''m not sure it adds to the shot.  i do like the flower (i have those at home, but can never remember the name), and it would make a good shot for texture as well, don''t you think? -- gr8photos (4)</td>', 'shame you missed the bee, i know they can be frustrating to photograph. :)  i''m wondering why you took the picture at the angle you did and rotated it this way.  i just turned it upright to look at it, but then it''s still a bit out of wack.  i find that a little confusing and i''m not sure it adds to the shot.  i do like the flower (i have those at home, but can never remember the name), and it would make a good shot for texture as well, don''t you think? -- gr8photos (4)', '2002-07-17 10:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
