(89948, 3422, 1759, '<td valign="top">Compositionally, this works and it is a fun shot also. However, there seems to be a lot of jpeg artifacting around the girls'' faces. I notice that your file size is very small, only 64K, but even so it should''t be this obvious. The photo could also be much sharper. I imported the photo to PhotoPaint and added some unsharp mask to verify this and it did help quite a lot. Be sure to shoot using the highest resolution your camera suports. If you import to a photo editor, do not save as a jpeg file until all of your edits are complete. Jpeg looses detail from a photo each time you save, so much better to save as a tiff file, which is lossless, then when all edits, resize, and sharpening have been done (in that order), save as a jpeg. If this doesn''t make sense, then I suggest asking on the Q&amp;A forum.</td>', 'Compositionally, this works and it is a fun shot also. However, there seems to be a lot of jpeg artifacting around the girls'' faces. I notice that your file size is very small, only 64K, but even so it should''t be this obvious. The photo could also be much sharper. I imported the photo to PhotoPaint and added some unsharp mask to verify this and it did help quite a lot. Be sure to shoot using the highest resolution your camera suports. If you import to a photo editor, do not save as a jpeg file until all of your edits are complete. Jpeg looses detail from a photo each time you save, so much better to save as a tiff file, which is lossless, then when all edits, resize, and sharpening have been done (in that order), save as a jpeg. If this doesn''t make sense, then I suggest asking on the Q&A forum.', '2002-07-21 17:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
